{
  "id": "mpwg-rala-2026-09",
  "name": "MPWG RALA",
  "author": "James",
  "version": "2026-09-rala-p2d",
  "description": "RALA ramp after the 2026-09-21 RadarScope side-by-sides (3:24 PM CT / 20:24Z and 3:36 PM CT, Johnson City / Dripping Springs / San Marcos). Continuous RGB+alpha interpolation, not nearest 5 dBZ steps. A probe of the southern storm edge was 12.0 dBZ and rendered as dull dark green; 10–15 dBZ are bright greens so that envelope reads as a wisp, not a dark rim. Yellow, orange, and red are spaced wider. High cores go through James magenta into a more saturated magenta. Very weak returns below 10 stay dark green. No cyan/aqua band. No-echo and missing stay alpha 0. No hard <15 cutoff. Composite keeps mpwg-clean-2026-09.",
  "units": "dBZ",
  "display_min_dbz": -32,
  "below_min": [0, 0, 0, 0],
